  "bodyText": "Home\nVisit Us\nExhibitions\nEvents\nOnline Talks\nOxfordshire’s Military Heritage in 50 Objects\nCollections\nBlog\nResearch\nLearning\nShop\nCart\nMy Account\nAbout\nBecome a Friend\nSupport Us\nRoom Hire\n\n01993 810 210\n\nfrontofhouse@sofo.org.uk\n\n  \nHome\nEvents\nExhibitions\nCollections\nFriends’ Membership\nVisit\nShop\nBasket\nMy Account\nOxfordshire’s Military Heritage in 50 Objects\nResearch\nLearning\nOnline Talks\nBlog\nSupport Us\nRoom Hire\nImage Services\nAbout\nBooks\nGifts\nLee Miller: A Woman at War – An evening with Ami Bouhassane | 7pm, Thurs 3 September 2026\n£15.00\n\n60 available\nLee Miller: A Woman at War - An evening with Ami Bouhassane | 7pm, Thurs 3 September 2026 quantity\nAdd to Cart\n\nA talk with Ami Bouhassane, author and co-director of Farleys House & Gallery, on the work and legacy of her grandmother, Lee Miller - celebrating the Lee Miller: A Woman at War exhibition at the Soldiers of Oxfordshire Museum (23 May - 13 September 2026).\n\nFarleys House & Gallery Ltd is the organisation managing the Lee Miller Archives, the Penrose Collection and Farleys House - the home of her grandparents, Lee Miller and Roland Penrose.\n\nAbout Ami Bouhassane\n\nManaging Director of Farleys House & Gallery Ltd, the organisation that manages the Lee Miller Archives and Farleys House, home of her grandparents Lee Miller and Roland Penrose. Through Farleys Bouhassane organises exhibitions in connection with their work, collections and contemporaries that are exhibited internationally as well as in the gallery spaces on site. Author, curator, podcast presenter and lecturer on both Miller and Penrose, Bouhassane has worked extensively with their material for over 28 years.\n\nHer first book ‘Lee Miller: A Life with Food, Friends and Recipes (2017) won 3 awards, including the IACP (International Association of Culinary Professionals) Jane Grigson award for scholarship. She is currently recording her third podcast series based on manuscripts and letters written by Miller held in the Lee Miller Archives.\n\nPublications:\n\nLee Miller in Print by Saskia Kampen-Prein, 2x contributed essays by Ami Bouhassane, Depot Boijmans Van Beuningen 2023. ISBN: 978 906 918 3305\nLee Miller. Man Ray: Fashion - Love – War, Skira 2023 Ed. Victoria Noel Johnson, contributed essay by Ami Bouhassane. ISBN: 978-8857244150\nLee Miller: Fashion in wartime Britain by Ami Bouhassane, Amber Butchart & Robin Muir, Lee Miller Archives Publishing, 2021 ISBN: 978-0953238989\nLee Miller: A Life with Food, Friends & Recipes by Ami Bouhassane, paperback, Lee Miller Archives publishing, 2021 ISBN: 978-1-914298-0-28\nGrim Glory: Lee Miller’s Britain at war by Ami Bouhassane, Lee Miller Archives Publishing, 2020, ISBN: 978-0953-23-8965\nLee Miller by Ami Bouhassane, Eiderdown Press, 2019, ISBN: 978-1-9160416-4-6\nPhotographer Lee Miller: The liberation of Denmark, May 1945, One of 2 contributors, essay ‘Lee Miller and the Mermaid’ by Ami Bouhassane, The Museum of National History at Frederiksberg, 2018. ISBN: 978-87-93049-21-5\nLee Miller: A Life with Food, Friends & Recipes by Ami Bouhassane, Grapefrukt Forlag with Penrose Film Productions Ltd, 2017 ISBN: 978-82-997574-5-4\n\nPhoto Credit: Jim Holden\n\nDate: 03-September-2026\nTime: 19:00\n\nLocation: Soldiers of Oxfordshire Museum (The Briefing Room), Park Street, Woodstock, OX20 1SN\nType: digital\n\nRelated products\nMeet Me at the Soldiers Museum | 2pm – 4pm | Thursday 2 July 2026\n£0.00 Add to cart\nSpy Princess: The Life Noor Inayat Khan with Shrabani Basu (Recorded Live at Ditchley Park)\n£9.00 Add to cart\nPOSTPONED Kinder | Show Time: 1pm\n£6.00 Read more\nPegasus Bridge: In Their Own Words (Online Talk)\n£0.00 Add to cart\n\nSoldiers of Oxfordshire Museum\nPark Street.\nWoodstock\nOxfordshire OX20 1SN\n\nPhone and Email:\nGeneral Enquiries & Event Tickets: 01993 810 211\nfrontofhouse@sofo.org.uk\n\nPrivacy Policy\nTerms and conditions",
